251
00:10:09,600 --> 00:10:10,680
"Listen and don't speak"

252
00:10:10,680 --> 00:10:11,280
Yes

253
00:10:11,280 --> 00:10:13,280
I think it was a very big mistake.

254
00:10:13,280 --> 00:10:14,860
Hear this and do not speak.

255
00:10:14,860 --> 00:10:16,760
To hear what and why not to speak.

256
00:10:16,760 --> 00:10:19,520
Whether this is what my mom or my dad used to
tell me,

257
00:10:19,520 --> 00:10:22,620
or some random person telling me what to do.

258
00:10:22,620 --> 00:10:25,220
I think we know pretty well where we live.

259
00:10:25,220 --> 00:10:27,860
We see what happens, no need to mention them
again.

260
00:10:27,860 --> 00:10:31,320
We've said it not on camera, we've said it to
each other.

261
00:10:31,320 --> 00:10:34,520
We have said them in general with too many
people and too many people have said them.

262
00:10:34,520 --> 00:10:40,520
Repeating all of it now would be too
mainstream, too basic.

263
00:10:40,520 --> 00:10:46,720
So I want to speak up when I don't like
something,

264
00:10:46,720 --> 00:10:49,720
though I don't want to open up that whole
discussion now.

265
00:10:49,720 --> 00:10:52,520
but because I have seen policemen provoking
people,

266
00:10:52,520 --> 00:10:56,080
protesters or whoever was there,

267
00:10:56,080 --> 00:11:00,960
and seen them provoke people to make an arrest
or two.

268
00:11:00,960 --> 00:11:03,160
Maybe they get a bonus; I don't care.

269
00:11:03,160 --> 00:11:05,880
I haven't experienced that personally.

270
00:11:05,880 --> 00:11:06,520
What have you seen in front of you?

271
00:11:06,520 --> 00:11:09,640
I have seen this before me at least 15-20
times.

272
00:11:09,640 --> 00:11:11,320
And some have seen more, too.

273
00:11:11,320 --> 00:11:14,280
I remember you were involved with football
grounds...

274
00:11:14,280 --> 00:11:15,280
Not anymore.

275
00:11:15,280 --> 00:11:17,280
Yes, yes, yes. It had to do with the field for
sure.

276
00:11:17,280 --> 00:11:18,280
You will have seen these.

277
00:11:18,280 --> 00:11:20,280
There was a lot of that going on,

278
00:11:20,280 --> 00:11:22,280
and I don't like it, man, that is

279
00:11:22,280 --> 00:11:25,280
Why provoke me to come

280
00:11:25,280 --> 00:11:27,280
and confront you, when you're

281
00:11:27,280 --> 00:11:29,280
twenty kilos heavier than me,

282
00:11:29,280 --> 00:11:32,280
armoured up in full gear,

283
00:11:32,280 --> 00:11:34,280
acting like a tough guy?

284
00:11:34,280 --> 00:11:36,280
A very basic question

285
00:11:36,280 --> 00:11:37,280
What's "bagioko," Giannis?

286
00:11:37,280 --> 00:11:38,580
The money.

287
00:11:38,580 --> 00:11:42,180
Thanks! You don't use that much slang.

288
00:11:42,180 --> 00:11:42,980
No, I haven't.

289
00:11:42,980 --> 00:11:44,780
Great wordplay, as always.

290
00:11:44,780 --> 00:11:48,380
For me personally word play is very important
in rap, okay?

291
00:11:48,380 --> 00:11:52,980
Sometimes I get lost in the slang, though. I
like that word.

292
00:11:53,980 --> 00:11:57,080
Especially on "Dafni," with all those flow
switches...

293
00:11:57,080 --> 00:11:57,580
Yes.

294
00:11:57,580 --> 00:12:00,280
You've got a complex pattern of flows.

295
00:12:00,280 --> 00:12:04,200
If someone mapped it out with notation and
analysis,

296
00:12:04,200 --> 00:12:07,120
they'd see how much work Giannis put into it.

297
00:12:07,120 --> 00:12:12,280
About the changing flows:

298
00:12:12,280 --> 00:12:15,480
Look, at some point in my life,

299
00:12:15,480 --> 00:12:19,320
I realised my delivery, going "duku, duku,
duku,"

300
00:12:19,320 --> 00:12:20,680
it was also a bit monotonous.

301
00:12:20,680 --> 00:12:25,240
Switching flows two or three times in a track

302
00:12:25,240 --> 00:12:27,880
is playing with the beat.

303
00:12:27,880 --> 00:12:32,480
and I like it a little more, i.e. you play
like this, you play differently, you play
slowly,

304
00:12:32,480 --> 00:12:37,280
Fast, sideways, winger, striker—everything, so
to speak!

305
00:12:37,280 --> 00:12:40,480
I really like that playfulness,

306
00:12:40,480 --> 00:12:44,080
the beat going slow, me going fast, bringing
it down, taking it up.

307
00:12:44,080 --> 00:12:45,780
I just like the flow too, you know.

308
00:12:45,780 --> 00:12:47,680
You're into dribbling, then?

309
00:12:47,680 --> 00:12:48,180
Yes, yes.

310
00:12:48,180 --> 00:12:48,680
Okay.

311
00:12:48,680 --> 00:12:51,120
Even though I was a defender, I've got the
dribbling!

312
00:12:51,120 --> 00:12:54,320
Another project I like, a really complete
project...

313
00:12:54,320 --> 00:12:56,640
I know you two will do more together.

314
00:12:56,640 --> 00:12:58,920
I really like "Hidden Message."

315
00:12:58,920 --> 00:13:02,760
And the project, all the direction, the flows,

316
00:13:02,760 --> 00:13:07,160
because there are too many. The whole set is
very nice.

317
00:13:07,160 --> 00:13:09,640
Something I noticed and liked:

318
00:13:09,640 --> 00:13:14,440
normally, people write in their own voice, or

319
00:13:14,440 --> 00:13:17,240
speak through someone else's perspective.

320
00:13:17,240 --> 00:13:18,940
But you know something? You are talking to the
listener.

321
00:13:18,940 --> 00:13:21,240
Rather than, "I do this, I do that."

322
00:13:21,240 --> 00:13:23,940
About that particular track:

323
00:13:23,940 --> 00:13:27,340
it's a long verse, with the chorus at the end.

324
00:13:27,340 --> 00:13:28,940
The whole verse is exactly what you describe,

325
00:13:28,940 --> 00:13:31,940
as if I'm a separate person talking to the
listener.

326
00:13:31,940 --> 00:13:33,940
In the chorus I'm talking to myself.

327
00:13:33,940 --> 00:13:40,140
Dimitris sings it, but I wrote it as me
talking to myself.

328
00:13:40,140 --> 00:13:42,740
You talk too much about the road. It's like
you're always on the road.

329
00:13:42,740 --> 00:13:45,140
I am on the road, because of my work too.

330
00:13:45,140 --> 00:13:45,940
You are on the way.

331
00:13:45,940 --> 00:13:49,940
Not just hanging around parks or whatever!

332
00:13:49,940 --> 00:13:52,340
No, you're literally on the road, how should I
say it?

333
00:13:52,340 --> 00:13:53,340
Yes.

334
00:13:53,340 --> 00:13:54,340
But I am literally.

335
00:13:54,340 --> 00:13:55,940
You can tell from the lyrics.

336
00:13:55,940 --> 00:13:56,540
But yeah, ok.

337
00:13:56,540 --> 00:13:58,340
You say, "I'm passing by, and I see..."

338
00:13:58,340 --> 00:14:00,340
"I'm doing this... passing by, seeing that..."

339
00:14:00,340 --> 00:14:01,540
You're talking about things

340
00:14:01,540 --> 00:14:02,840
which you see around you,

341
00:14:02,840 --> 00:14:04,640
in passing, and capturing them.

342
00:14:04,640 --> 00:14:05,640
That brief glimpse,

343
00:14:05,640 --> 00:14:07,540
where someone else might not notice anything,

344
00:14:07,540 --> 00:14:09,940
you turn it into something,

345
00:14:09,940 --> 00:14:11,140
rather than letting it go,

346
00:14:11,140 --> 00:14:12,140
something useful to you.

347
00:14:12,140 --> 00:14:14,140
Observing without even realising.

348
00:14:14,140 --> 00:14:16,140
It's what stays with me.

349
00:14:16,140 --> 00:14:18,140
And I want you to tell me because you have
done...

350
00:14:18,140 --> 00:14:20,140
I see Dimitris that he is everywhere,

351
00:14:20,140 --> 00:14:23,140
and he's played an important role so far.

352
00:14:23,140 --> 00:14:26,140
Dude, Dimitris I can't tell you

353
00:14:26,140 --> 00:14:29,140
how much respect I have for him.

354
00:14:29,140 --> 00:14:31,140
Shout-out to Dimitris Tsekeris.

355
00:14:31,140 --> 00:14:33,140
It's not just Dimitris.

356
00:14:33,140 --> 00:14:36,140
We knew each other by sight.

357
00:14:36,140 --> 00:14:39,660
Eventually we met at a place where he was,

358
00:14:39,660 --> 00:14:41,760
And you know, we get to talk a little bit,
man, and that.

359
00:14:41,760 --> 00:14:45,020
and he said he recorded at home.

360
00:14:45,020 --> 00:14:46,660
He gave me something he'd worked on to hear.

361
00:14:46,660 --> 00:14:49,720
And I say, ok, nice. And we close the session.

362
00:14:49,720 --> 00:14:51,700
That session, by the way, was "Biri Biri."

363
00:14:51,700 --> 00:14:54,700
In the studio, it wasn't just Dimitris's work,

364
00:14:54,700 --> 00:14:58,300
not just the great mixing and mastering.

365
00:14:58,300 --> 00:15:01,020
It was our chemistry.

366
00:15:01,020 --> 00:15:01,660
The Vibe.

367
00:15:01,660 --> 00:15:04,220
Chemistry in general. I mean, many times
it's...

368
00:15:04,220 --> 00:15:06,420
I do something, and he says, "You're inside my
head!"

369
00:15:06,420 --> 00:15:08,100
This is very useful.

370
00:15:08,100 --> 00:15:09,900
Beyond being useful,

371
00:15:09,900 --> 00:15:12,620
there's a different connection with that
person.

372
00:15:12,620 --> 00:15:14,260
Got it, ok, so it's...

373
00:15:14,260 --> 00:15:15,260
So yeah...

374
00:15:15,260 --> 00:15:16,260
You inspire each other.

375
00:15:16,260 --> 00:15:19,260
Yeah, and ideas start flowing.

376
00:15:19,260 --> 00:15:21,260
You will see a lot in the near future.

377
00:15:21,260 --> 00:15:24,260
Ideas are coming, but that doesn't mean
they're all mine.

378
00:15:24,260 --> 00:15:28,260
Someone gets an idea, either me, or Dimitris
and anyone else.

379
00:15:28,260 --> 00:15:32,260
He tells me something, I say something and we
take it and build it straight away.

380
00:15:32,260 --> 00:15:37,260
My question about this piece lately is why is
the video etc what it is?

381
00:15:37,260 --> 00:15:41,260
Two people, one in each shot, blindfolded.

382
00:15:41,260 --> 00:15:43,860
Are we talking about the image, where we are
blindfolded?

383
00:15:43,860 --> 00:15:49,260
Being blindfolded in "Hidden Message"
represents going in blind.

384
00:15:49,260 --> 00:15:51,260
The point is not that we just go blindly.

385
00:15:51,260 --> 00:15:53,860
I often feel that we are running to get
nowhere.

386
00:15:53,860 --> 00:15:55,860
That's basically what the song says.

387
00:15:55,860 --> 00:16:00,020
Then there's the track we made with Tzimos...

388
00:16:00,020 --> 00:16:03,700
Is this a crossover episode?

389
00:16:03,700 --> 00:16:08,020
When "Doryforos" came out, you say "a little
dance," while Tzimos

390
00:16:08,020 --> 00:16:10,020
says "a little space."

391
00:16:10,020 --> 00:16:12,020
And you go with "dance" instead!

392
00:16:12,020 --> 00:16:16,260
And something you do and based on my notes
again man you do it often

393
00:16:16,260 --> 00:16:18,260
You talk a lot about your people.

394
00:16:18,260 --> 00:16:18,760
Yes.

395
00:16:18,760 --> 00:16:22,360
Apart from talking about being on the road
again and going back and forth, anything...

396
00:16:22,360 --> 00:16:22,860
Yes, yes, yes.

397
00:16:22,860 --> 00:16:24,660
You talk a lot about them.

398
00:16:24,660 --> 00:16:26,260
I don't think you do it like other rappers.

399
00:16:26,260 --> 00:16:28,960
People who are here,

400
00:16:28,960 --> 00:16:32,260
and people who aren't here, or who are
elsewhere,

401
00:16:32,260 --> 00:16:34,860
who support you even if they aren't there
every day.

402
00:16:34,860 --> 00:16:35,760
from what I understand

403
00:16:35,760 --> 00:16:39,460
What support do you get for your rap from the
people around you?

404
00:16:39,460 --> 00:16:43,460
Do you mean people I don't know?

405
00:16:43,460 --> 00:16:46,960
Both people you know and people you don't.
Rappers don't always get support.

406
00:16:46,960 --> 00:16:51,960
I can't say much about strangers; there aren't
many yet.

407
00:16:51,960 --> 00:16:53,960
Actually, they aren't really strangers...

408
00:16:53,960 --> 00:16:58,460
I'd call them friends now.

409
00:16:58,460 --> 00:17:02,220
I mean someone who came to a live show and
heard us.

410
00:17:02,220 --> 00:17:04,780
That feedback's been good.

411
00:17:04,780 --> 00:17:09,780
From the people I know and from the people
very close to me,

412
00:17:09,780 --> 00:17:13,220
it's positive. I know it's positive

413
00:17:13,220 --> 00:17:14,420
when they tell me my mistakes.

414
00:17:14,420 --> 00:17:17,660
Rather than telling me it's great,

415
00:17:17,660 --> 00:17:20,060
then saying something else to other people.

416
00:17:20,060 --> 00:17:24,220
When I hear from my friend, from my best
friend, from my mother, from my father man,

417
00:17:24,220 --> 00:17:29,220
"You could say that differently, or do it this
way."

418
00:17:30,540 --> 00:17:32,980
Even if I say, "That's what I wanted to say,
how I wanted to say it."

419
00:17:33,100 --> 00:17:36,940
They've still taken the time to look closely.

420
00:17:36,980 --> 00:17:38,780
Not just saying,

421
00:17:38,860 --> 00:17:40,180
"You've messed it up," or whatever.

422
00:17:40,180 --> 00:17:42,540
I don't know... that you said something very
wrong, or anything

423
00:17:42,540 --> 00:17:45,540
They've heard some little detail,

424
00:17:45,540 --> 00:17:48,540
and ask, "Couldn't you also do that?"

425
00:17:48,540 --> 00:17:51,540
"Or do it this way?" That means a lot to me.

426
00:17:51,540 --> 00:17:53,540
I wrote a verse and read it to a friend.

427
00:17:53,540 --> 00:17:55,540
I read it to him, he says "you can do better."

428
00:17:55,540 --> 00:17:56,540
And I thought, "Man, that's..."

429
00:17:56,540 --> 00:17:57,540
That's honesty, man.

430
00:17:57,540 --> 00:17:59,540
We want these people.

431
00:17:59,540 --> 00:18:01,540
If he'd told me it was the best verse he'd
heard,

432
00:18:01,540 --> 00:18:04,340
I might have released it. Maybe not, but...

433
00:18:04,340 --> 00:18:06,040
You never know

434
00:18:06,040 --> 00:18:08,840
One question, since I can see it: what's with
Bilbao?

435
00:18:08,840 --> 00:18:11,640
Well, Bilbao. MBJ had gone to Bilbao.

436
00:18:11,640 --> 00:18:14,240
He called, "Want a Bilbao shirt?" Of course!

437
00:18:14,240 --> 00:18:17,740
It's like Crete in Greece,

438
00:18:17,740 --> 00:18:19,640
in terms of the mindset.

439
00:18:19,640 --> 00:18:21,840
You go somewhere and say, I'm not Greek, I'm
Cretan.

440
00:18:21,840 --> 00:18:25,340
For a reason. Instead of saying "I'm from
Spain," they'll say, "I'm from Bilbao."

441
00:18:25,340 --> 00:18:27,540
He has the corresponding pride, so to speak.

442
00:18:27,540 --> 00:18:29,340
I really like people like that, man

443
00:18:29,340 --> 00:18:33,540
So, and before we go do the session, I have a
question to ask everyone man.

444
00:18:33,540 --> 00:18:34,040
Yes.

445
00:18:34,040 --> 00:18:37,340
I'd like to ask your favourite rapper,
regardless of nationality,

446
00:18:37,340 --> 00:18:39,780
and your favourite line, regardless of who
wrote it.

447
00:18:39,780 --> 00:18:45,580
Look now and see, for a favorite rapper I
don't think I can easily tell you.

448
00:18:45,580 --> 00:18:49,220
I don't have one favourite above everyone
else.

449
00:18:49,220 --> 00:18:53,860
I've got plenty of influences, obviously:

450
00:18:53,860 --> 00:18:57,860
MF DOOM, Wu-Tang, Mobb Deep, and many others.

451
00:18:57,860 --> 00:19:01,260
Can't tell dude exactly.

452
00:19:01,260 --> 00:19:06,620
Maybe Nas clicks with me a little more.

453
00:19:06,620 --> 00:19:07,360
Yes

454
00:19:07,360 --> 00:19:09,900
Caught you off guard! You weren't expecting
that.

455
00:19:09,900 --> 00:19:11,600
We haven't talked much about this part

456
00:19:11,600 --> 00:19:12,320
For the Nas

457
00:19:12,320 --> 00:19:12,820
Yes, yes

458
00:19:12,820 --> 00:19:13,320
But...

459
00:19:13,320 --> 00:19:14,720
Since the other day you were saying...

460
00:19:14,720 --> 00:19:15,220
It is not...

461
00:19:16,360 --> 00:19:21,360
There's something about Nas that takes him
that bit further for me.

462
00:19:21,360 --> 00:19:22,460
I know what he has

463
00:19:22,460 --> 00:19:25,020
He talks like you, about what he sees outside.

464
00:19:25,020 --> 00:19:26,320
Yeah dude that's it

465
00:19:26,320 --> 00:19:28,120
His flows,

466
00:19:28,120 --> 00:19:28,860
Okay

467
00:19:28,860 --> 00:19:34,860
and his bars... So, if I have to pick one,

468
00:19:34,860 --> 00:19:38,860
I'll say Nas. But I'm still not completely
certain.

469
00:19:38,860 --> 00:19:40,860
Sorry, before we move on from Nas...

470
00:19:40,860 --> 00:19:44,860
There's a "The World Is Yours" poster here.
This wasn't staged!

471
00:19:44,860 --> 00:19:46,860
Nas... and Nas!

472
00:19:46,860 --> 00:19:50,860
Though people might think of Tony Montana when
they see it.

473
00:19:50,860 --> 00:19:52,860
What is this, why did they show it?

474
00:19:52,860 --> 00:19:54,860
You also asked for a favourite line.

475
00:19:54,860 --> 00:19:55,860
A favourite line, yes.

476
00:19:55,860 --> 00:20:01,620
It isn't complicated, but it says a lot.

477
00:20:01,620 --> 00:20:04,100
It is from Psycho Realm, in Stone Garden.

478
00:20:04,100 --> 00:20:05,900
Why is this song everywhere, man?

479
00:20:05,900 --> 00:20:08,260
Why dude, okay.

480
00:20:08,260 --> 00:20:11,700
Two tracks blew my mind

481
00:20:11,700 --> 00:20:13,820
when I was a kid. That was it.

482
00:20:13,820 --> 00:20:16,300
And there was one that's not rap, but it
doesn't matter,

483
00:20:16,300 --> 00:20:17,820
was Stairway to Heaven, by Led Zeppelin.

484
00:20:17,820 --> 00:20:19,860
Two tracks that would make sense

485
00:20:19,860 --> 00:20:21,940
as ones that could blow your mind!

486
00:20:21,940 --> 00:20:25,660
My favourite line is, "Keep your eyes wide
open and alive."

487
00:20:25,660 --> 00:20:29,260
It isn't anything wild, but it says so much.

488
00:20:29,260 --> 00:20:32,860
Sick Jacken delivers it beautifully. [imitates
his voice]

489
00:20:32,860 --> 00:20:37,100
It's the delivery too, but the line says so
much at once.

490
00:20:37,100 --> 00:20:38,660
It meant a lot to me.

491
00:20:38,660 --> 00:20:41,980
I expected you to say Nas, but I get it.

492
00:20:41,980 --> 00:20:45,620
I don't have any tattoos. If I got one, it'd
be that line.

493
00:20:45,620 --> 00:20:46,940
Yes. ok

494
00:20:46,940 --> 00:20:48,780
That line has meant a lot to me.

495
00:20:48,780 --> 00:20:51,660
Ready to go and make something?

496
00:20:51,660 --> 00:20:52,780
Let's head home and see what we can do.

497
00:20:52,780 --> 00:20:53,540
Of course.

498
00:20:53,540 --> 00:20:54,060
Think we've got this?

499
00:20:54,060 --> 00:20:54,700
Yes.

500
00:20:54,700 --> 00:20:55,260
Good.

501
00:20:55,260 --> 00:20:55,780
Good.

502
00:21:02,400 --> 00:21:04,600
Here we are. We're not on the rooftop,

503
00:21:04,600 --> 00:21:05,520
because it took us...

504
00:21:05,520 --> 00:21:06,600
The conversation was...

505
00:21:06,600 --> 00:21:07,880
Constructive, you could say.

506
00:21:07,880 --> 00:21:10,880
It took half an hour, and we'd run into the
evening.

507
00:21:10,880 --> 00:21:14,380
We're inside, in that DIY setup we talked
about.

508
00:21:14,380 --> 00:21:16,880
